===
*-ical* is sometimes used at the end of a sentence when in another position *-ic* would be more natural (*An idea more true than -ical,* cf. *A no less true than poetic idea*); & *-ic* is sometimes jocularly substituted for *-ical* (*The -ic effusions of an*
>>>

